417
01:57:48,720 --> 01:57:51,200
I gradually shorten the exams over time.

418
01:57:51,200 --> 01:57:53,480
But essentially, the questions that

419
01:57:53,480 --> 01:57:58,000
are asked will be very similar in form and difficulty.

420
01:57:58,000 --> 01:58:01,480
See, then in terms of the breakdown of material,

421
01:58:01,480 --> 01:58:04,080
when I write the exams, I try to get about 50%

422
01:58:04,080 --> 01:58:08,120
of the questions from lecture, about 30% from homework,

423
01:58:08,120 --> 01:58:11,120
and about 20% from the readings.

424
01:58:11,120 --> 01:58:12,640
So remember this class has readings.

425
01:58:12,640 --> 01:58:14,120
They're on a syllabus.

426
01:58:14,120 --> 01:58:16,120
You may have been postponing them.

427
01:58:16,120 --> 01:58:19,000
But you will be asked.

428
01:58:19,000 --> 01:58:21,240
And I often like to go and write a question that

429
01:58:21,240 --> 01:58:22,400
